8:46:53Z","updated_at":"2026-08-12T17:20:28Z","closed_at":"2026-08-12T17:20:28Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nFound in 4.7 stable.\n\nReproducible in 4.8 dev2, first version reproducible is 4.6 beta1\n\nNot reproducible in 4.6 dev6 and earlier\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.stable - macOS Sequoia (15.7.4) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M1 (Apple7) - Apple M1 (8 threads) - 8.00 GiB memory - CoreAudio (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nGodot crashes sometimes when double-clicking a signal to open the connect dialogue. This happens inconsistently but I found a way to consistently reproduce the crash, the crash can sometimes happen without the specific steps below but it's very inconsistent.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open node_2d.tscn and select its root node.\n2. Navigate to the signal tab of the inspector dock.\n3. Hover mouse over a signal in the signals dock\n4. Rapidly alternate double-clicking to open the 'connect signal' window and using cmd + w to close the opened window. Do this 3-4 times, the button will stop responding to clicks.\n5. Press cmd + w again to close the scene without shifting the mouse. \n6. Reopen the scene and select the node\n7. Double-click on a signal again to trigger the crash\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c5851240-300d-4bff-a161-af3f4f45c78f\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nA project with one saved scene is enough to recreate the crash.\n[crash-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/30261095/crash-test.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id"